build 11: a TEMPO switch next to the BPM: 1/2x | 1x | 2x, each showing the BPM it plays at (65 / 130 / 260 when FL is at 130). It stays locked to FL's bars; DRAG MIDI lands in FL exactly as you hear it (written at FL's tempo, a 2x bar fills half an FL bar), DRAG AUDIO is rendered as you hear it with the BPM in the file name; saved with the project, a new Ghosty Beats starts at 1x. GROOVE moved to the third row next to SONG MODE. A click anywhere on the sound's waveform (bottom right) plays it, and its WAV drag is now exactly what you hear: the kit's tune and the track's settings at your project's sample rate (it used to be the raw sample, at another pitch). Version 3.1.2.
build 10: opens at 1200 x 760, a size that fits FL Studio's plug-in window on a 1440 x 900 MacBook Pro (still resizable; always this size when it opens), and a new Ghosty Beats is always a fresh start: NORMALISE, the MIDI channel, FOCUS and SOUNDS FROM no longer carry over from the last Ghosty Beats (a project keeps its own); only the look is remembered. Built and installed on Brandon's own Mac. Version 3.1.1.
build 12: NEON, a 5th look (the look button: BLACK -> PURPLE -> LIGHT -> GHOST -> NEON). A faded, hand-painted 1995 cyberpunk city in the rain behind everything: smoggy sky, weathered towers fading into the haze, neon signs that bleed into the wet air and flicker now and then, power lines, live rain in the header, film grain; no floating ghosts in NEON; more neon ads and lit billboards whose light runs down through the rain, the wet street's neon reflections rippling under the bottom strip; GHOSTY BEATS redrawn as a neon sign on a weathered plate (pink GHOSTY, teal BEATS, the headphones ghost as an amber tube; the Y flickers now and then); muted petroleum teal / olive / dirty amber / charcoal controls, lit steps glow like neon tubes, the playhead is amber. Remembered like the other looks. BLACK / PURPLE / LIGHT / GHOST are pixel-identical to before. Version 3.2.0.
build 13: fills the whole window: no more black bars at the sides (or top / bottom) when FL's window is a different shape. The design is scaled to fit and the layout widens (or grows taller) to use the rest: the grid, the lanes and the rainy city stretch to the edges, the right panel, macros and header buttons move out to the edge. NEON is now the look a new Ghosty Beats opens in on a computer that never picked one (a saved look is still remembered). Version 3.2.1.
build 14: two looks only: NEON (the rainy city, the default) and a new LIGHT: sumi-e ink + watercolour on warm washi paper (charcoal brush lines, muted vermilion / indigo / moss / blossom pink washes, a pale moon, bamboo and a blossom branch in the header, petals drifting down that swirl on the hits, panel ink lines that scribble for a moment on every hit). BLACK, PURPLE, the old LIGHT and GHOST are removed (an old saved look opens as NEON). The expanded SEQUENCER page no longer shows the mini tracker: the lanes take the full width. Version 3.3.0.
build 15: SOUNDS: a new ALL folder at the top of the list (searches every sound); the search box now searches only the folder you're on: on KICKS it finds kicks, on a bank or pack (MY · SOUTHSIDE...) it finds only that pack's sounds, so typing "hat" there gives that pack's hats. The empty search box says what it will search. Version 3.3.1.
build 16: FL Studio no longer risks a crash when you close it (the pixel font is no longer freed after FL has shut its font system down). Version 3.3.2.
build 17: LIGHT look toned down: softer parchment paper instead of bright cream (less blinding), darker text and clearer button outlines; the GHOSTY BEATS logo is now a light, faded print on the paper (no black ink plate). Version 3.3.3.
